Package: sqc
Title: Companion Tools for a Statistical Quality Control Course
Version: 0.13.1
Authors@R: person("Tyler", "Grimes", email = "tyler.grimes.unf@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Control chart constants (d2, d3, c4, A2, D3, D4, and others),
    Shewhart X-bar and R charts and Levey-Jennings charts with the Westgard
    rules drawn with ggplot2, a run-length simulator for the average run
    length of control rules, single sampling plans for acceptance sampling
    (OC curves, producer's and consumer's risk, average outgoing quality,
    and a plan search), ANOVA estimators of the variance components of a
    one-way random effects model and Gage R&R for a crossed two-factor study
    (with simulators), process capability indices with confidence intervals and
    a sampling distribution simulator, CUSUM and EWMA charts for small shifts
    with their average run lengths (integral equations and simulation),
    likelihood-ratio CUSUMs for counts and for risk-adjusted outcomes, p, np, c,
    and u charts with normal or exact probability limits, funnel plots for
    comparing institutions (with overdispersion adjustments) and their
    simulation, a Pareto chart, autocorrelation (ACF) plots, AR(1) simulation and
    residual charts for dependent data, Hotelling's T-squared charts for
    correlated variables (with the control ellipse, a comparison of the box of
    separate charts with the ellipse, and a simulation of the limits when the
    covariance is estimated), randomized plans and the simulation of blocking, randomization, and
    pseudoreplication, two-level factorial designs and fractions with their
    effects, alias structure, power, and a comparison with one factor at a time,
    cause-and-effect diagrams, and the example datasets used in the lecture
    slides and notes.
